# The image holds what runs and nothing else, so everything is left out and the few
# files the build needs are let back in. No tests, .venv, .git, .claude, .vscode or
# out/; and no scripts/ or sql/: seeding is done from a checkout, with uv. The page is
# let in as its sources, without the node_modules and dist of a machine that has built
# it: the Node stage runs npm ci and builds its own. (The last pattern that matches a
# path decides, so the two exclusions come after web/ is let in.)
*
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!.python-version
!README.md
!src/
!web/
web/node_modules
web/dist
